   COMMIT
   DEF: Permanently save the transaction changes

   INPUT:
   START TRANSACTION;

   UPDATE student
   SET age = 26
   WHERE id = 1;

   COMMIT;

   OUTPUT: Changes are permanently saved
   REAL: Confirm a successful payment/order


   ROLLBACK
   DEF: Undo changes made in the current transaction

   INPUT:
   START TRANSACTION;

   UPDATE student
   SET age = 30
   WHERE id = 1;

   ROLLBACK;

   OUTPUT: Update is undone
   REAL: Cancel changes when an error occurs


   IMPORTANT:
   COMMIT   → Changes SAVE
   ROLLBACK → Changes UNDO


   FLOW:
   START TRANSACTION
          ↓
      INSERT / UPDATE / DELETE
          ↓
      ┌───────────────┐
      ↓               ↓
    COMMIT         ROLLBACK
      ↓               ↓
     SAVE            UNDO
*/
