/* =========================
   16. PRIMARY KEY / FOREIGN KEY
   =========================
   DEF: Define unique identity and relationships between tables
   WHEN: Identify records and connect tables
   WHERE: Relational databases, user/order/product systems


   PRIMARY KEY
   DEF: Uniquely identifies each row in a table
   RULE: UNIQUE + NOT NULL

   INPUT:
   CREATE TABLE student (
       id INT PRIMARY KEY,
       name VARCHAR(50),
       age INT
   );

   OUTPUT: Every student has a unique id
   REAL: Student ID uniquely identifies each student


   FOREIGN KEY
   DEF: Connects one table to another table
   RULE: References a PRIMARY KEY (or UNIQUE key) in another table

   INPUT:
   CREATE TABLE orders (
       order_id INT PRIMARY KEY,
       student_id INT,
       FOREIGN KEY (student_id) REFERENCES student(id)
   );

   OUTPUT: orders.student_id is connected to student.id
   REAL: Connect an order with the student who placed it


   EXAMPLE RELATIONSHIP:

   student
   ┌────┬───────┐
   │ id │ name  │
   ├────┼───────┤
   │ 1  │ Anup  │
   │ 2  │ Rahul │
   └────┴───────┘
          ↑
          │
   FOREIGN KEY
          │
   orders
   ┌──────────┬────────────┐
   │ order_id │ student_id │
   ├──────────┼────────────┤
   │ 101      │ 1          │
   │ 102      │ 2          │
   └──────────┴────────────┘


   IMPORTANT:
   PRIMARY KEY → Row ki unique identity
   FOREIGN KEY → Tables ke beech relationship
*/
/* =========================
   17. JOINS
   =========================
   DEF: Combine data from multiple tables
   WHEN: Related data from different tables is needed
   WHERE: Reports, dashboards, relational data


   INNER JOIN
   DEF: Returns only matching rows from both tables

   INPUT: SELECT student.name, orders.order_id
          FROM student
          INNER JOIN orders
          ON student.id = orders.student_id;

   OUTPUT: Students who have matching orders
   REAL: Show users who have placed orders


   LEFT JOIN
   DEF: Returns all rows from left table
        and matching rows from right table

   INPUT: SELECT student.name, orders.order_id
          FROM student
          LEFT JOIN orders
          ON student.id = orders.student_id;

   OUTPUT: All students, including students without orders
   REAL: Show all users and their orders


   RIGHT JOIN
   DEF: Returns all rows from right table
        and matching rows from left table

   INPUT: SELECT student.name, orders.order_id
          FROM student
          RIGHT JOIN orders
          ON student.id = orders.student_id;

   OUTPUT: All orders, including orders without matching students
   REAL: Show all orders with available student details


   CROSS JOIN
   DEF: Returns every possible combination of rows

   INPUT: SELECT student.name, course.course_name
          FROM student
          CROSS JOIN course;

   OUTPUT: Every student combined with every course
   REAL: Generate all possible student-course combinations


   JOIN MULTIPLE TABLES
   DEF: Combine 3 or more related tables

   INPUT: SELECT student.name,
                 orders.order_id,
                 course.course_name
          FROM student
          INNER JOIN orders
          ON student.id = orders.student_id
          INNER JOIN course
          ON student.id = course.student_id;

   OUTPUT: Data combined from student, orders and course
   REAL: Create a report using data from multiple tables


   QUICK SUMMARY:

   INNER JOIN → Only matching rows
   LEFT JOIN  → All left + matching right
   RIGHT JOIN → All right + matching left
   CROSS JOIN → Every possible combination
   MULTIPLE JOIN → Join 3 or more tables
*/
/* =========================
